# Render Pipeline

En WebGPU, el *render pipeline* combina vertex y fragment shaders y describe cómo se dibujan los triángulos.

## Definir shaders WGSL
```ts
const vertexWGSL = /*wgsl*/`
[[stage(vertex)]]
fn main([[location(0)]] pos : vec4<f32>) -> [[builtin(position)]] vec4<f32> {
  return pos;
}
`;
const fragmentWGSL = /*wgsl*/`
[[stage(fragment)]]
fn main() -> [[location(0)]] vec4<f32> {
  return vec4<f32>(0.0, 0.5, 1.0, 1.0); // azul
}
`;
```

## Crear módulos y pipeline
```ts
const device = await navigator.gpu.requestAdapter().then(a => a.requestDevice());
const vsModule = device.createShaderModule({code: vertexWGSL});
const fsModule = device.createShaderModule({code: fragmentWGSL});

const pipeline = device.createRenderPipeline({
  vertex: {module: vsModule, entryPoint: 'main'},
  fragment: {module: fsModule, entryPoint: 'main', targets: [{format: 'bgra8unorm'}]},
  primitive: {topology: 'triangle-list'},
});
```

## Uso en un render pass
```ts
const commandEncoder = device.createCommandEncoder();
const textureView = context.getCurrentTexture().createView();
const pass = commandEncoder.beginRenderPass({colorAttachments: [{view: textureView, loadOp: 'clear', clearValue: {r:0,g:0,b:0,a:1}, storeOp: 'store'}]});
pass.setPipeline(pipeline);
pass.draw(3, 1, 0, 0); // dibuja un triángulo
pass.end();
device.queue.submit([commandEncoder.finish()]);
```

> **Tip**: Usa `pipeline.getBindGroupLayout(0)` para conectar bind groups al pipeline.
